Role Description

Role purpose

Provide central quality assurance and constructive challenge for the technical, operational,&nbsp;data and resilience aspects of BRT scenarios.&nbsp;The role will assess whether systems, interfaces, batch processes, data, recovery arrangements and operational controls are sufficiently tested and evidenced to support readiness decisions.

Key responsibilities&nbsp;

• Own relevant Central scenarios;

• Review and quality-assure technical acceptance criteria created or co-created by Value Stream SMEs;

• Check whether criteria are technically testable and linked to observable evidence;

• Review evidence from systems, interfaces, batch runs, reconciliations, logs and reports;

• Assess whether evidence relates to the correct:

• System

• Environment

• Data set

• Process step

• Failure condition

• Recovery outcome

• Challenge unsupported technical coverage claims;

• Identify limitations relating to:

• Test environments

• Test data

• Failure injection

• Production monitoring

• Batch scheduling

• System availability

• Support the design of targeted BRT tests for technical and operational gaps;

• Review resilience and recovery evidence, including alternate processing and manual workarounds;

• Support gap prioritisation and risk-acceptance recommendations.

Skills and Expertise

Essential skills and experience

• Experience in complex banking system testing, migration or test assurance;

• Strong understanding of system interfaces and cross-system dependencies;

• Experience with data migration, reconciliation and reference integrity;

• Experience reviewing test evidence and traceability;

• Knowledge of batch processing, end-of-day processing and exception handling;

• Understanding of reruns, duplicate processing, recovery and operational controls;

• Ability to assess logs, reports, reconciliations, audit trails and runbooks;

• Ability to translate technical gaps into focused, executable tests;

• Strong analytical and documentation skills;

• Fluency in German and English.

Priority domain knowledge&nbsp;

• Batch and end-of-day processing;

• System interfaces and data flows;

• Migration data and reconciliation;

• Operational recovery and resilience testing;

• The role does not need to be a software developer, system architect or detailed infrastructure specialist. The key requirement is sound technical test judgement and the ability to determine whether evidence proves the claimed business and operational outcome.

